# The base's pad pressure, control: a plain held BD pad (no roll) sends its pressure to the sound's
# aftertouch and to MIDI poly pressure, as stock does. The aftertouch target the sound reads is one word per
# track at 0x800067de (BD first), written as the pad's pressure byte times 128 (stock's setter 0x4011f490);
# on MIDI it goes out as `An note pressure/2` when PAD DEST and PRESSURE DST send to USB (INT+EXT, the
# default). Plays BD and leaves its aftertouch at 0.
name: pad-plain
state: changes

midi m begin
pad BD down 100
wait 300
pad BD pressure 60
wait 300
mem at60 0x800067de 2
pad BD pressure 30
wait 300
mem at30 0x800067de 2
pad BD pressure 0
pad BD up
wait 300
midi m end
expect at60 == 1e00
expect at30 == 0f00
expect m.notes == 1
expect m.polyat > 1
